"Vulkan: Sync dirty disabled active attributes" (crbugs 573933450,
571059182 and 580173680, not public; no CVE listed yet): ANGLE's Vulkan
back-end left a vertex attribute that was disabled while still active in the
program pointing at its old buffer when a zero-count multidraw skipped the
deferred cleanup, so a later draw could read the freed buffer (use after
free). Disabled attributes, active or not, are now always reset to the empty
buffer. ANGLE main commit e473507a8a86fa7c0aa6e419e2a8fd81283e1bfa
(2026-10-29), merged on 2026-11-02 to 157
(751417514a521b2e92d6928260c62122138824d3, after the 157.0.8103.37 tag; also
proposed for 156). This is the 157 merge, without its tests. Drop it once a
157 tag has it.

